{
  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "How this graph works",
      "content": "Two branches start at the Data Input.\n1. Word vectors (top): a preparation step. It trains word2vec on the posts and saves one vector per vocabulary token. It is not wired to the model: the saved file is the connection.\n2. Training (bottom): Tokenizer -> Split -> Loader -> Embedding -> LSTM -> Dense -> CrossEntropy -> AdamW. The Embedding loads the saved vectors as its starting weights.\nThe Tokenizer, the Word vectors node and the Embedding share one vocabulary file (sentiment_analysis_vocab.txt, 5,000 tokens), so row i of the vectors is the vector of token id i.\nRun the Word vectors node first, then Train. Result 2026-10-14 (GTX 1050 Ti): best validation accuracy 73.8% (early stop at epoch 10).",
      "pos_x": -60.0,
      "pos_y": -520.0,
      "width": 900.0,
      "height": 230.0,
      "minimized": false
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "The vocabulary file",
      "content": "Made by prepare_sentiment_analysis_demo.py (examples/cyxgraph/Sentiment analysis):\n- each post lowercased and split into words AND single punctuation marks (regex [A-Za-z0-9_]+ | [^\\w\\s]), so ',' '.' '?' are tokens too;\n- tokens counted over all posts; kept if seen at least 5 times;\n- sorted most frequent first (ties A-Z), cut to 5,000 including the 4 special tokens;\n- written one per line: line number = token id. [PAD]=0, [UNK]=1, [BOS]=2, [EOS]=3, then i, '.', to, and, ',', the, my ...\nThe Tokenizer reads it to turn words into ids; the Word vectors node reads it to order its rows.",
      "pos_x": 980.0,
      "pos_y": -520.0,
      "width": 820.0,
      "height": 230.0,
      "minimized": false
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Word vectors node vs Embedding layer",
      "content": "Word vectors: data preparation, runs once before training, learns from neighbouring words without labels, output is a file that does not change during training.\nEmbedding: part of the model, runs on every batch, learns from the sentiment labels through the loss, its numbers keep changing (Freeze off).\nThe word vectors are a general dictionary built from all the posts; the Embedding is the model's own copy, refined for telling the 7 labels apart. Random start (Weights: Random) is the comparison to see what the word vectors add.",
      "pos_x": 1880.0,
      "pos_y": -520.0,
      "width": 820.0,
      "height": 230.0,
      "minimized": false
    }
  ],
